WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:15.616
Summer, was passing too quickly and although he was having fun with the girls, Laurie felt restless.

2
00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:18.937
He wanted to travel and visit his friends in Europe.

3
00:00:19.738 --> 00:00:25.119
Thinking about this, he sat on the window ledge, looking across at his unusually quiet neighbors one day.

4
00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:27.480
"What is she up to?"

5
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:31.254
Laurie wondered as he suddenly caught sight of Jo coming out of the house.

6
00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:35.736
He was about to call out to her when he noticed her acting very strangely.

7
00:00:35.756 --> 00:00:38.318
"Where is that girl going?"

8
00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.418
he asked himself.

9
00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:45.642
Jo tiptoed out of the house, being careful not to slam the door, and quietly walked down the

10
00:00:45.682 --> 00:00:52.105
path. She was carrying a large envelope, which she held tightly as if her life depended upon it.

11
00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:56.528
She walked briskly down the street, looking behind her every few minutes.

12
00:00:57.688 --> 00:00:58.708
"She's sneaking out!

13
00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:01.049
Well, we can't have that!"

14
00:01:01.369 --> 00:01:02.110
Laurie chuckled.

15
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.631
He got up and hurried downstairs.

16
00:01:05.551 --> 00:01:09.792
Whatever Jo was trying to hide, he was determined to find out.

17
00:01:11.253 --> 00:01:13.494
Laurie found Jo's pace irregular.

18
00:01:14.214 --> 00:01:19.516
Sometimes she skipped, but other times she slowed to a crawl as if she were thinking about something.

19
00:01:20.364 --> 00:01:25.568
People like her were the most difficult to follow since you never knew if they would stop suddenly,

20
00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:27.970
turn around, and notice they were being followed.

21
00:01:28.831 --> 00:01:31.634
Still, Laurie thought his disguise was a good one.

22
00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.756
He wore his grandfather's hat and walked with a cane.

23
00:01:36.378 --> 00:01:42.543
Jo headed into town, passing the dentist's office then the grocer's, and walked toward the billiard room, but

24
00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:48.668
to Laurie's great relief, she passed that disreputable place and went inside an office located next to it.

25
00:01:49.424 --> 00:01:50.945
"Where on earth is she going?"

26
00:01:51.385 --> 00:01:52.926
Laurie was dying to know.

27
00:01:53.806 --> 00:01:58.908
Positioning himself in front of a dress shop, he pretended to be interested in the latest colors of

28
00:01:58.948 --> 00:02:01.469
the season, while he waited for Jo to come out.

29
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:08.312
Laurie wondered how many more times he could raise his hat in greeting to each passing lady, as

30
00:02:08.372 --> 00:02:10.653
was the custom for gentlemen to do in those days.

31
00:02:11.593 --> 00:02:17.356
"Good day, Madam," he said, imitating his grandfather's voice as two elderly women approached the shop he was

32
00:02:17.376 --> 00:02:18.216
standing in front of.

33
00:02:19.136 --> 00:02:23.879
Keeping one eye on the office where his friend had gone, Laurie politely opened the door for the

34
00:02:23.919 --> 00:02:31.525
ladies. To his delight, across the street, another door was opening at that moment, and soon Jo appeared

35
00:02:31.565 --> 00:02:33.746
looking excited, happy, and relieved.

36
00:02:35.247 --> 00:02:37.949
Laurie noted that she was no longer carrying the envelope.

37
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.093
Having successfully ushered the ladies inside the store, Laurie ran toward Jo.

38
00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:47.276
Raising his hat, he shouted, "Excuse me, Miss, one moment, please."

39
00:02:48.092 --> 00:02:52.615
Jo turned around to see a gentleman running (quite quickly, in her opinion) in her direction.

40
00:02:53.275 --> 00:02:57.657
He looked very familiar and his voice sounded like "Laurie?"

41
00:02:58.078 --> 00:03:00.239
she asked, surprised to see her friend in town.

42
00:03:00.259 --> 00:03:02.940
"Of course it's me," he replied.

43
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.921
"What are you doing here?"

44
00:03:05.141 --> 00:03:08.723
Jo asked as she pulled the hat from his hand and tried it on herself.

45
00:03:08.743 --> 00:03:11.245
"Never mind me, Jo March.

46
00:03:11.545 --> 00:03:12.445
What are you hiding?"

47
00:03:12.726 --> 00:03:13.826
Laurie demanded to know.

48
00:03:14.947 --> 00:03:18.752
Flushing, Jo looked away and shrugged, "I don't know what you're talking about."

49
00:03:18.773 --> 00:03:21.853
"Don't deny it, Jo, I saw you.

50
00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:25.955
I followed you here, so I know you went inside that office.

51
00:03:26.455 --> 00:03:26.915
What is it?

52
00:03:27.315 --> 00:03:28.155
What is your secret?

53
00:03:28.215 --> 00:03:28.655
Tell me!"

54
00:03:29.035 --> 00:03:30.216
Laurie nearly shouted.

55
00:03:31.516 --> 00:03:37.038
Jo crossed her arms stubbornly and said, "That's very naughty of you to follow me, Theodore Laurence.

56
00:03:37.838 --> 00:03:40.439
And I don't have to tell you anything if I don't want to."

57
00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:46.481
Laurie chewed on his lower lip then with a twinkle in his eye said, "If you tell me

58
00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.562
your secret, I'll tell you mine."

59
00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.304
Jo considered his offer then stuck out her hand.

60
00:03:52.324 --> 00:03:55.606
"Deal, but you must promise not to tell a soul."

61
00:03:56.526 --> 00:03:58.548
Laurie swore he wouldn't say a word.

62
00:03:59.308 --> 00:04:04.771
Rubbing her hands together, Jo said breathlessly, "I sold two stories to the newspaper.

63
00:04:04.791 --> 00:04:06.952
They bought my stories, Laurie!"

64
00:04:07.953 --> 00:04:12.636
Laurie stared at his friend, then let out a loud shout of joy and gave her a big

65
00:04:12.676 --> 00:04:17.862
hug. The two women who had entered the store now came out and seeing this public display of

66
00:04:17.922 --> 00:04:21.583
affection, covered their mouths and shook their heads disapprovingly.

67
00:04:22.524 --> 00:04:27.886
Ignoring them, Laurie and Jo linked arms and ran down the street, still cheering and making a lot

68
00:04:27.906 --> 00:04:28.386
of noise.

69
00:04:31.548 --> 00:04:36.470
As they got closer to their neighborhood, Jo turned to Laurie and said, "Now you have to tell

70
00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:37.370
me your secret."

71
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.551
Laurie covered his mouth and held back a giggle.

72
00:04:40.571 --> 00:04:42.956
"I don't know "Laurie!

73
00:04:43.156 --> 00:04:44.057
We had a deal!"

74
00:04:44.157 --> 00:04:45.477
Jo said, grabbing his arm.

75
00:04:46.138 --> 00:04:46.658
"What is it?

76
00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:47.458
Tell me!"

77
00:04:47.478 --> 00:04:53.701
"Okay, but remember, you mustn't repeat what I'm about to tell you," he said seriously.

78
00:04:53.721 --> 00:04:56.242
"Laurie, tell me already!"

79
00:04:56.582 --> 00:04:57.943
Jo nearly screamed.

80
00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:01.924
"Brookes has a crush on Laurie's voice drifted off.

81
00:05:02.785 --> 00:05:06.186
Jo, her eyes growing bigger and more alarmed, whispered, "Who?

82
00:05:07.007 --> 00:05:10.108
Meg?" Laurie nodded, grinning.

83
00:05:10.632 --> 00:05:14.936
"It's more than a crush, actually; Brookes is in love with your sister."

84
00:05:15.956 --> 00:05:21.441
Jo stopped, her feet suddenly heavy and heart weighed down with this unexpected revelation.

85
00:05:21.461 --> 00:05:24.443
"No, that's impossible."

86
00:05:24.904 --> 00:05:25.864
Jo shook her head.

87
00:05:26.645 --> 00:05:31.769
"Why? Meg is a very beautiful girl and Brookes isn't a bad chap," said Laurie.

88
00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:38.741
Although she knew it would happen eventually, Jo refused to believe that one day her sisters would get

89
00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.402
married and have their own families.

90
00:05:41.483 --> 00:05:42.703
"Laurie, are you sure?"

91
00:05:43.063 --> 00:05:45.844
Jo asked, hoping this was one of his pranks.

92
00:05:46.825 --> 00:05:52.007
Laurie, however, nodded and said, "He wrote it in his diary, which happened to be open one day,

93
00:05:52.107 --> 00:05:55.848
and in passing, I "You read his diary?

94
00:05:56.309 --> 00:05:57.369
You little crook!"

95
00:05:58.109 --> 00:05:59.510
Jo punched Laurie in the arm.

96
00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:01.391
"I didn't read the whole thing.

97
00:06:01.451 --> 00:06:02.691
I just glanced at it.

98
00:06:02.711 --> 00:06:06.434
Ouch! That hurt, Jo," he moaned, rubbing his sore arm.

99
00:06:07.535 --> 00:06:13.480
Jo pushed him farther away; her once light and carefree steps were now burdened with what Laurie had

100
00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.200
just told her.

101
00:06:15.802 --> 00:06:20.826
Two days later, Mother and all the girls, except for Jo, were sitting quietly in the living room,

102
00:06:20.986 --> 00:06:22.528
all occupied with their own work.

103
00:06:23.388 --> 00:06:28.273
Their peaceful afternoon, however, was suddenly interrupted by a noisy commotion in the foyer.

104
00:06:28.293 --> 00:06:31.836
"My word," Mother exclaimed, putting down her sewing.

105
00:06:32.848 --> 00:06:38.293
At that moment, Jo, the cause of the deafening sounds, burst into the room, swinging a newspaper in

106
00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:40.775
the air, and dashing around as if she were on fire.

107
00:06:40.795 --> 00:06:43.637
"Jo! What on earth!

108
00:06:43.957 --> 00:06:45.178
Calm down, child!"

109
00:06:45.479 --> 00:06:46.499
Mother spoke sternly.

110
00:06:46.519 --> 00:06:51.403
"Sorry, Mother," gasped Jo, as she ran past and pecked her mother on the cheek.

111
00:06:52.284 --> 00:06:55.327
"Jo! What's so exciting about that newspaper?"

112
00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:56.267
called out Amy.

113
00:06:57.028 --> 00:07:01.732
Finally Jo collapsed onto the floor next to Beth, who gently took the paper from her.

114
00:07:02.468 --> 00:07:04.489
It was open to a particular page.

115
00:07:04.509 --> 00:07:10.873
"Like Mother, Like Daughter," Beth read, "by Josephine March.

116
00:07:11.894 --> 00:07:14.195
Jo! This is your story!"

117
00:07:15.456 --> 00:07:19.358
Soon the entire house was filled with loud cheers and a great deal of shouting.

118
00:07:20.078 --> 00:07:22.139
Jo was now a published writer.

119
00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:27.582
As everyone came around to give her a hug, she held on more tightly and longer to Meg.

120
00:07:28.403 --> 00:07:33.267
Now Jo's secret was out of the bag but she wondered how much longer she could keep Laurie's

121
00:07:33.307 --> 00:07:34.308
secret from being known.

122
00:07:35.249 --> 00:07:37.672
Jo hoped it would be a long, long time.
